Git Reference Guide (Categorized)
1. Setup & Configuration
git config --global user.name "Your Name" — Set global username

git config --global user.email "your.email@example.com" — Set global email address

git config --global core.editor "editor_name" — Set default text editor

git config --global merge.tool "tool_name" — Set default merge tool

git config --global diff.tool "tool_name" — Set default diff tool

2. Getting & Creating Projects
git clone repository_url — Clone a repository from a remote source

git remote add origin repository_url — Add a remote repository link

3. Basic Snapshotting & Status
git status — Check the status of the repository

git add . — Add all changes to the staging area

git commit -m "Your commit message" — Commit staged changes with a message

git diff — Show changes between commits, working tree, etc.

4. Branching & Merging
git branch — List all local branches

git checkout branch_name — Switch to a specific branch

git switch branch_name — Modern alternative to checkout for switching branches

git merge branch_name — Merge a specific branch into the current branch

git rebase branch_name — Reapply commits on top of another base tip

5. Remote Synchronization
git fetch — Download objects and refs from another repository

git pull — Fetch from and integrate with another repository or a local branch

git push — Update remote refs along with associated objects

6. Inspection & History
git log — View commit history

git show commit_hash — Show metadata and content changes of a specific commit

7. Advanced Workflow & Troubleshooting
git reset --hard commit_hash — Reset current HEAD to a specific state, discarding changes

git stash — Save modified, tracked changes in a dirty working directory away

git stash pop — Apply stashed changes and remove them from the stash list

git cherry-pick commit_hash — Apply the changes introduced by an existing commit

git revert commit_hash — Create a new commit that undoes the changes of a target commit

git clean -fd — Remove untracked files and directories from the working tree

git tag tag_name — Create a static point-in-time tag reference

8. Custom Aliases & Shortcuts
git config --global alias.co checkout — Alias for git checkout

git config --global alias.br branch — Alias for git branch

git config --global alias.ci commit — Alias for git commit

git config --global alias.st status — Alias for git status

git config --global alias.lg "log --oneline --graph --all" — Alias for a concise log view

git config --global alias.unstage "reset HEAD --" — Alias to unstage files

git config --global alias.last "log -1 HEAD" — Alias to show the last commit

git config --global alias.visual "!gitk" — Alias to launch the gitk visualizer